---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import InterestForm from "../components/InterestForm.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Andorra entrepreneur residence (D.4)"
  description="The Government’s D.4 page for participants in entrepreneur programmes: economy-ministry resolution, 90-day presence, one-year grants."
  path="/entrepreneur-residence"
>
  <section class="page-header">
    <h1>Entrepreneur-programme residence (D.4)</h1>
    <p>
      The Government still publishes a dedicated D.4 page. It is not a
      general start-up visa. It is residence for people admitted to the
      entrepreneur programmes that the economy ministry promotes.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="prose">
    <div class="notice">
      <p>
        Source:
        <a
          href="https://www.govern.ad/ca/tematiques/immigracio/residencia/residencia-per-a-participants-en-programes-per-a-emprenedors"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          >D.4. Residència per a participants en programes per a
          emprenedors — Govern d’Andorra</a
        >.
        Financial means are those “set by regulation”. If the official
        page changes, use that page.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2>What the Government says D.4 is</h2>
    <p>
      A newcomer may apply, under current law, whose work does not
      require a fixed geographic location and who uses
      telecommunications and technology, and the tools chosen to take
      part in the programme for foreign entrepreneurs promoted by the
      ministry responsible for the economy, and who establishes
      principal and effective residence in Andorra for at least 90 days
      per calendar year.
    </p>

    <h2>How long the official page says it lasts</h2>
    <p>
      The initial residence authorisation is granted for one year,
      renewable for successive periods of the same length. That is
      shorter than the two-year D.1 / D.3 cycle on neighbouring pages.
      Confirm it on the live D.4 text.
    </p>

    <h2>Documents listed (non-exhaustive)</h2>
    <p>
      The official list is expressly “enunciative and not limiting”. It
      includes, among other items:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>passport, or for EU/EEA nationals a national identity card;</li>
      <li>
        criminal-record certificates from the country of origin, of
        nationality and of residence;
      </li>
      <li>a recent colour photograph to the stated format;</li>
      <li>
        a favourable resolution from the ministry responsible for the
        economy qualifying the person as someone whose work needs no
        fixed location and uses telecommunications and technology, as
        set by regulation;
      </li>
      <li>
        evidence of owning or renting a habitable dwelling, or of having
        started a purchase that must complete within one year of the
        residence application;
      </li>
      <li>civil-status documents as listed on the page;</li>
      <li>a written commitment to the 90-day presence;</li>
      <li>
        sufficient economic means as set by regulation, for the
        applicant and dependants;
      </li>
      <li>
        illness and incapacity cover for Andorra for the life of the
        residence (the page states a narrower illness-only cover for
        minors and for people over sixty);
      </li>
      <li>
        the applicant’s signature, and that of persons for whom
        residence is requested, committing to the 90-day presence and
        to keeping the insurance in force;
      </li>
      <li>
        Comú registration within one month of the grant, and proof of
        that registration within the same period.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Foreign official documents must carry a Hague apostille or be
      otherwise legalised. That sentence is on the same page.
    </p>
    <p>
      Related:
      <a href="/digital-nomad">D.3</a>,
      <a href="/passive-residency">D.1</a>,
      <a href="/company-active-residency">J.1</a>,
      <a href="/become-a-resident">all permit types</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <InterestForm
    intro="Leave an email if you are looking at D.4 and want an introduction to counsel."
    source="entrepreneur-residence"
  />
</Base>
